## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/contrast.html
- Summary (EN): The Contrast node changes the tonal spread of a layer, VDB or attribute around a chosen midpoint. Raising Contrast spreads values outward from the midpoint, lowering it pulls them back toward it.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Contrast étire ou resserre les valeurs d'une couche autour d'un centre choisi, avec un réglage par canal et des bornes optionnelles.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer, VDB or attribute to modify", "contrast (optional): per-pixel control scaling the Contrast amount", "mask (optional): per-pixel control scaling the Mask amount"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by source", "Mask: blend of new value with original, default 1", "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: channels affected", "Contrast: 1 leaves the image unchanged, 0 sets all values to the centre", "Contrast Center: pivot point of the adjustment", "Per-channel Contrast and offset pairs for Red, Green, Blue, Alpha (offset not explained in detail on the page)", "Clamp Below Zero: stops values going negative", "Clamp Above One: limits values to 1, useful for masks; HDR images may need values above 1", "Treat RGBA as Premultiplied: un-premultiplies, applies contrast, re-premultiplies"]

- Caveats: ["Black values can be pushed below zero unless Clamp Below Zero is enabled", "Without Treat RGBA as Premultiplied, a fixed pivot can make low-coverage premultiplied pixels too dark"]

